{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/81969-on-combat","id":81969,"title":"On Combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-28T23:57:46-08:00","id":81969,"title":"On Combat","content":"And <i>WoD: Combat</i>. So, we're wrapping up our 18 month Vampire game, and my players want to try their hands at a Hunters game. I'm compiling all my hand-written notes and formatting them into a new <i>Combat</i> book (<b>NOTE</b>: this is neither approved nor endorsed by CCP/WW/OP. This is for my own personal use). I thought I'd get some feedback from you helpful forum people, to make it more, I don't know, <i>universal</i>. Fix and tweak things, you know. I am not including the splat-specific martial arts and the like; this is just a repository for weapons, munitions, that kind of stuff. Plus rules for esoterica (like having to take a turn to pause between firing white phosphorus rounds from your shotgun, lest you melt the barrel). It's in the outline stages currently, but I'll be posting updates when I tinker around with it.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your help.<br /> <br /> Link is here:<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15LGlQ2iY6Pvt0Vqtwwcl1X9ApfaVZ7oLd6kk_jZlwNc/pub\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD20: Combat!</a><br /> <br /> 7/3 - The section I dread will cause the most criticism has been posted, and I am working on an example of play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 05-15-2014, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T23:55:23-08:00","id":83816,"title":"","content":"I very much approve this idea, because weapons and their stats are terribly inconsistent all over the various books.<br /> <br /> How in depth are you going to go with weapons? Like, how many of them? Because I fiddled with giving stats for various weapon classes, but got overwhelmed. Happy to share my classes if you\u2019d like. Also, you can see the lists of the various weapons and maneuvers, etc. and where they are described from the Werewolf and related books from my Werewolf reference spreadsheet here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"> Amazon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I would also include the different types of Lethal damage from the Dark Ages rules, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T00:37:29-08:00","id":83839,"title":"","content":"Drinkin' whiskey, makin' lists... This thing's up to 2100 words now - all the sidebars are done, 99% of the shotgun stuff. Whew.<br /> <br /> rderekp - Heh, that's awesome. I'm off to bed now, but I will definitely take a look at that stuff tomorrow. I'm kind of stuck on melee weapons - how to categorize and classify them, all that. For Firearms, I'm mainly separating it by caliber - since it's the size of the bullet that really matters, mostly. I would honestly appreciate any help offered. Also, I had no idea that Dark Ages had different types of Lethal damages. Now I'll have to see if that fits in the whole paradigm...<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T04:34:11-08:00","id":83899,"title":"","content":"Nothing, did you not like the way that Combat categorized weapons? (Bladed/Blunt/Flexible/etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T11:54:21-08:00","id":84089,"title":"","content":"The problem with <i>World of Darkness: Combat</i> is that the maneuvers are often incredibly expensive (2 Willpower points for Neckbreaker -- which isn't even that great of an attack and requires a successful grapple/clinch first? Please), and they're not so good anyway. I've used <i>WoD: Combat</i> in pretty much every game I've run, and I make everybody buy the maneuvers with combat points and so on -- but they just end up doing regular attacks, or not applying their bonuses; but my NPCs do -- and it really doesn't feel decisive. Keep in mind, when there's a penalty, I'd be on top of it and remind people, and if it occurred to me, I'd remind them about their bonuses as well... but knowing a martial art, and doing roundhouse kick or an uppercut, or whatever... it just doesn't really matter in light of the fact that the various games provide super powers which are perfectly effective attacks in and of themselves.<br /> <br /> I think that if I were to run a game using the cWoD system, but where no one had superpowers (or, at least, very limited superpowers -- like everyone is a ghoul or some kind of not-so-badass sorcerer/hedge wizard) then maybe the combat system would come into play more.<br /> <br /> What it comes down to is that the martial arts and special moves and such in <i>WoD: Combat</i> should have been more like those particular things in <i>Exalted</i>, rather than White Wolf's frequently forgotten <i>Street Fighter</i> RPG.<br /> <br /> With regards to weapon stats and the like -- I just don't think there was enough variation between the various weapons. The game would have benefited more from having restrictions on the use of certain weapons. For example, if you have Melee 1 because you avoided and/or perpetrated numerous shankings in prison, you should not be able to pick up a katana and be able to avail yourself of it's full stats. Those stats, if I am not mistaken (this is off the dome) are Str+3 (Damage); Accuracy +1; Initiative +1. That's great and all -- but if your Melee 1 is justified by a passing familiarity with a wielding a sharp piece of glass wrapped in duct tape, or a toothbrush that has had the bristles removed and a razor melted in the head in the bristles place... how can you justify being able to use the katana to its full potential. A game that appreciates this is (I believe), <i>Shadowrun</i>. In that game one's melee/firearms weapon skill (whatever they're called) dictates to what degree a given weapon's stats apply -- e.g., the gun may be 4d6 to hit, but your skill of XX may only allow you to use 2d6; and by that same token, no matter how skillful you are, you can never roll more than 4d6 to hit with that weapon.<br /> <br /> I apologize for going off on this rant or whatever, but I've always run fairly cinematic games that run a little heavier on combat, and it's bothersome to me that there's was never very much support for that style of gameplay in cWoD (and what little support there was, <i>WoD: Combat</i>, feels incredibly half-assed, and I would guess wasn't play-tested very much).<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>Thank you for taking it upon yourself to try to fix and address problems. I hope to have some useful feedback for you regarding same, as overall fixes to the system are badly needed; and from my first, cursory review of the document, it looks like this is going in the correct direction (or, at least in the direction that seems correct to me, in my humble and inexpert opinion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 03-04-2014, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T00:08:43-08:00","id":84440,"title":"","content":"Options. The name of the game is options, for players and Storytellers alike. In complete opposition to that statement, I'm not inclined to include a lot about armor. I think the core books handle that well enough. If someone else wanted to try their hand at them, I wouldn't say no.<br /> <br /> It's been a long day, and I'm drinking whiskey while cleaning up a few things in the document. I've only been able to spend about an hour on this thing tonight, apologies.<br /> <br /> rderekp - I can hit the link, and get the option to download your text, but when I open it, it's gibberish (like a .txt file). Maybe I have the wrong software?<br /> <br /> Derzhuzad - I didn't realize that the older book separated them in that way. I didn't notice it when I scanned the book taking notes - I'll have to go back with a more observant eye. But that seems like a good categorization, yeah.<br /> <br /> CaptOtter - Thanks. It's always nice to know it's appreciated. I'm completely throwing out the Power Points stuff, along with the splat-oriented martial arts. To be honest, I agree with you - the normal stuff is often as good or better - and really, I'm not smart enough to completely re-write the Werewolf one (which is probably the coolest one).<br /> <br /> Again, thank you all for your time and feedback.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T00:23:10-08:00","id":85872,"title":"","content":"Bumping to get eyeballs on it, since I finished the quick combat section.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T18:43:26-07:00","id":88548,"title":"","content":"Just took a look at the progress, you are really move along its great! Did you settle on how you wanted to divide up weaponry yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T13:29:10-07:00","id":89010,"title":"","content":"My biggest recommendation would be to take into consideration the context behind the weapons one might get to use. A lot of games that introduce melee weapons to a modern setting (World of Darkness included) do so in a vacuum. You're given rapiers next to greatswords, for instance, along with stat lines... but no understanding as to why we, as a species, went from big lengths of iron and steel to smaller, thinner, pointier weapons. That would lead into recommendation number two, which would be to base what weapons can and can't do in a game based on what they could and could not do in real life. There are all sorts of fun resources out there that can show us what sort of trauma most popular weapons could inflict. Similarly, there are many resources that can tell you how effective most such weapons were against armor, how they were used to get around such defenses, how damaging parrying other weapons or bashing blades against plate armor could be, etc. The same easily holds true for modern firearms and body armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2303-phoebus","name":"Phoebus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T16:44:24-07:00","id":89117,"title":"","content":"Does anyone has a simple i guess &quot;Hack&quot; for improoving &quot;sneak attacks&quot;? just not getting the chance to abort your action so that then you can try to dodge/block/parry doesnt seem like what should be a huge advantage in combat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/122-talum","name":"Talum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar122_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T12:11:29-07:00","id":89635,"title":"","content":"@nothing, It\u2019s an Excel spreadsheet. If you need a different format, drop me an PM with your email and I will send it to you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When I was fiddling with doing something similar with making a better weapon list, here are some of the categories I came up with. Hopefully maybe this helps:<br /> <br /> <b>Archaic Weapons (examples):</b><ul><li>Axe, Hand (Adze, Brush axe, Hand saw, Hatchet)</li> <li>Axe, Throwing (Francisca, Tomahawk)</li> <li>Axe, Two-Handed (Bardiche, Battle axe, Broadaxe, Dane axe, Labrys, Shepherd\u2019s axe)</li> <li>Bayonet</li> <li>Blade, Throwing (Chakram, Shuriken, Throwing knife)</li> <li>Blowgun</li> <li>BolasBattle pick, Horseman\u2019s pick, Martel de Fer, Pickaxe</li> <li>Bow, Compound</li> <li>Bow, Longbow (Daiky\u016b, Decurve bow, Deflex bow, English Longbow, Welsh Longbow)</li> <li>Bow, Recurved (Cable-backed bow, Hungarian bow, Perso-Parthian bow)</li> <li>Bow, Short (Hanky\u016b, Mongol bow, Turkish bow)</li> <li>Chain, Bladed (Kusarigama)</li> <li>Chain, Blunt (Chain, Meteor hammer, Slungshot)</li> <li>Chainsaw</li> <li>Club, Metal (Crowbar, Dumbbell, Flashlight, Frying pan, Golf club, Hammer, Lead pipe, Mace, Morning star, Scepter, Sledgehammer, Tire iron, Trash can, Wrench)</li> <li>Club, Simple (2\u00d74, Barstool, Baseball bat, Baton, Bludgeon, Bottle, Brick, Broom handle, Cane, Chair, Club, Cricket bat, Cudgel, Eskrima sticks, Hockey stick, Jitte, Macana, Mere, Millwall brick, Nightstick, Pistol whip, Pool cue, Rock, Sap, Shillealgh, Tonfa, Truncheon, War club)</li> <li>Club, Throwing (Boomerang, Knobkerrie, Thrown stone)</li> <li>Crossbow, Large (Crossbow, Arbalest)</li> <li>Crossbow, Small (Commando crossbow, Pistol crossbow)</li> <li>Dagger, Curved (Kris)</li> <li>Dagger, Straight (Arkansas toothpick, Bowie knife, Dagger, Fire poker, Fighting knife, French nail, Hunting dagger, Ice pick, Knightly dagger, Main gauche, Naval dirk, Parrying dagger, Scottish dirk, Scratch awl, Stiletto, Trench dagger, Trench knife)</li> <li>Drill, Power (Hand drill, Industrial drill)</li> <li>Fan, War (Iron fan, Korean fan)</li> <li>Flail (Ball and chain, Chainlock)</li> <li>Garotte</li> <li>Hand / Fist Blade (Bagh nakh, Katar, Punch Knife, Push dagger, Wind-and-fire wheel)</li> <li>Hand / Fist Blunt (Brass knuckles,Cestus, Gauntlet, Knuckle dusters, Roll of quarters, Sap gloves)</li> <li>Jackhammer</li> <li>Knife (ASEK, Butterfly knife, Butterfly sword, Combat knife, Commando knife, Folding knife, KA-BAR, Kampfmesser, Meat cleaver, Navy knife,</li> <li>Lasso</li> <li>Nunchaku</li> <li>Pick (Battle pick, Horseman\u2019s pick, Martel de Fer, Pickaxe)</li> <li>Polearm, Axe (English long axe, Hafted axe, Pollaxe)</li> <li>Polearm, Bill (Bill, Bill-Guisarme, Bill-Hook, Fauchard, Scythe, War Scythe)</li> <li>Polearm, Fork (Man catcher, Military fork, Pitchfork, Steel rake)</li> <li>Polearm, Glaive (Glaive, Guan do, Guisarme, Naginata, Voulge)</li> <li>Polearm, Halberd</li> <li>Polearm, Hammer (Bec de Corbin, Lucerne hammer)</li> <li>Polearm, Lance</li> <li>Polearm, Partisan (Spetum, Swordstaff)</li> <li>Polearm, Trident</li> <li>Shield (Kite shield, Riot shield, Trashcan lid)</li> <li>Sickle</li> <li>Sling (Staff sling)</li> <li>Slingshot</li> <li>Spear (Boar spear, Pike, Ranseur, Shovel, Spade)</li> <li>Spear, Thrown (Atlatl, Harpoon, Javelin)</li> <li>Staff (B\u014d, Quarterstaff)</li> <li>Stake</li> <li>Sword, Axe-like (Machete)</li> <li>Sword, One-handed Curved (Backsword, Cavalry saber, Cutlass, Falchion, Hunting sword, Khopesh, Kukri, Mameluke sword, Navy cutlass, Officer\u2019s sword, Saber)</li> <li>Sword, One-handed Straight (Basket-hilted Sword, Broadsword, \u00c9p\u00e9e, Foil, Flamberge, Heavy cavalry sword, Infantry sword, Longsword, Ninjat\u014d, Rapier, Sword cane)</li> <li>Sword, Short Curved (Wakizashi)</li> <li>Sword, Short Straight (Baselard, Foot artillery sword, Gladius, Small sword, Straight sword)</li> <li>Sword, Two-handed Curved (Dao, Katana, Shin gunt\u014d)</li> <li>Sword, Two-handed Straight (Boar sword, Claymore, Executioner\u2019s sword, Flambard, Hand-and-a-half sword, Two-handed sword, Zweih\u00e4nder)</li> <li>War-Hammer (Horseman\u2019s hammer, War hammer)</li> <li>Whip (Bullwhip, Car antenna, Cat o\u2019 Nine Tails, Crop, Stockwhip)</li> </ul><b>Gun list to come soon.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T13:56:22-07:00","id":89694,"title":"","content":"On combat maneuvres: The uppercut is listed as doing lethal damage, with the justification that it is targeted at the head, yet the eye/nose/throat strike does not, though it would seem this is likewise directed at the head.<br /> <br /> 3.1.4 Accuracy: Keep in mind that lowering difficulty usually has a much larger impact than simply adding a dice to the dicepool, due to the fact it changes the statistics for every dice in the pool. This would mean essentially that weapons/maneuvres with bonuses to accuracy are generally better than those without.<br /> <br /> As for the list provided by rderkp, it isn't bad, but there are a few corrections to be made:<br /> <br /> Flamberge is a technique/design in blade design. It can be applied to a number of different sword designs, from daggers to zweihanders (the Flambard, as listed). As such, it is a bit of a misnomer to have as types of swords.<br /> <br /> The Falchion is nothing like a sabre, and behaves somewhere between an axe and a sword. I would suggest grouping it with the machete.<br /> <br /> The long-sword (langes schwert) is technically the name for a fighting style, in which one uses both hands on the sword, i.e using the type of swords commonly referred to as &quot;bastard&quot; or &quot;hand-and-a-half&quot;. The use of longsword as a type of sword is purely a RPG phenomenon. Similarly, &quot;heavy cavalry sword&quot; and &quot;infantry sword&quot; are not something I am familiar with. The term most commonly used for a sword intended for use with one hand (other than simply &quot;sword&quot;) is arming sword.<br /> <br /> Finally, as someone else noted, there is a greater difference between the fencing style of an epee or a foil and the medieval sword, than there is between one handed swords, be they small, curved (use from horseback notwithstanding) or axe-like. This is due to the very different defensive weapons of the times. I'd suggest making a diffrentation there, rather than anywhere else (with the possible exeption of two-handed, since that is quite a different ball game, too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T23:55:28-07:00","id":89999,"title":"","content":"I've only barely started to read through this and I have to say already I think you're going in the wrong direction. Streamlining the system and removing the separate hit and damage and soak rolls is what NWoD did. If you want streamlined, I suggest NWoD. If you want realistic, stick with OWoD, where the decision to dodge the sword is incompatible with the action of bullrushing your opponent, or at least made more difficult (split actions). I highly suggest against the streamlining approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T00:16:29-07:00","id":90008,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with the above. In fact, the whole &quot;streamlining&quot; (or dumbing-down, as I like to call it), part is a bit confusing, since the rest seems to aim at increasing granularity (more maneuvres etc.). So, it would help, I think if the aim was perhaps stated a bit more clearly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T00:56:55-07:00","id":90024,"title":"","content":"I couldn't agree more with the two previous posters,.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","name":"harlokin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T10:45:10-07:00","id":90335,"title":"","content":"Couple of quick things while I'm taking a break from real work -<br /> <br /> Derzhuzad - I'm thinking I'm just going to lay everything out, then categorize. Get all the information down first.<br /> <br /> Phoebus - I'm not sure what you're trying to say. You would like a historiography to go along with it? Unfortuantely, I am not qualified to write something like that, and other people have written better texts than I could attempt. I am just trying to provide a list of resources.<br /> <br /> Talum - A free attack could mean life or death, especially when you add in all the modifiers (flanking, aimed, etc.).<br /> <br /> rderekp - Ah, I was trying to open it in a word processing program. That explains it. I'll pop it open in Google spreadsheet later. Thanks! (And looking forward to that gun list.)<br /> <br /> HOD - Some things here need longer explanations, so... Uppercut vs. Eye strike: The difference is in intent and training, where a professionally trained boxer is trying to knock someone out, while the drunk college kid is making a desperate attempt. There is also a bit of design wiggle-room for ST's, so that they may determine if they would like the strike to be Lethal or not. As always, I am open to suggestions either way. Accuracy: I am aware of the curve in the numbers regarding dicepools, but difficulty can not drop below 4, ever, for any reason. It's another design choice - giving players an option of adding more dice or lowering difficulty. Smarter players will, of course, lower difficulty any chance they get, but there are still some people that love rolling two handfuls of dice instead. Granularity: I'm not looking to divide, subdivide, further sub-subdivide... As I responded to Phoebus, I'm just trying to provide a list of resources for the players that say &quot;I think an uppercut should do this!&quot; or &quot;I have a melee of 4 and spent 30 years in prison making shanks, of course I know how to use a katana!&quot;<br /> <br /> killersquirrel59 - Thank you for the advice, but I don't personally care for nWoD. My troupe and I have extensively playtested this option every week for 18 months, and I just thought I'd share with anyone looking to make combat go a bit faster, smoother, and less math-intensive (because I have players that actively hate math, but will gleefully do it when it's simple subtraction and they're trying not to die). We've found that it's equally as &quot;realistic&quot; as any roleplaying system. Under the RAW, one has the chance of rolling 10+ successes to-hit, and then rolling 0 successes on damage, which is what prompted this whole thing months ago, and really just doesn't seem fair to me (or my troupe).<br /> <br /> harlokin - Okay. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously, thank you all for your feedback - every critique makes me rethink the process, reexamine the results, and see if maybe something couldn't be done in a better manner. I know that if I can't muster an adequate defense for a design choice, then it definitely needs to be reworked. Based on comments, I've already revised several things. However, I am also aware that I can't make everyone happy - and I have no desire to - but Golden Rule, right? If you don't like something, don't use it, or work it until it fits your game better. But if you find something you like, excellent! I'm glad to have helped. One gamer to another, I really do appreciate the time and responses, because time is one true non-refundable resource.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> Edit: HOD - I think I might erase that sentence about the head and lethal damage. It's supposed to be just flavor-text anyway, and I'm inclined to leave it a little more ambiguous, more open to Storyteller interpretation. Unless empty-handed attacks targeting the head are still bashing? I don't have the books with me right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 03-13-2014, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T12:01:08-07:00","id":90364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/81969-on-combat?p=90335#post90335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple of quick things while I'm taking a break from real work -<br /> <br /> HOD - Some things here need longer explanations, so... Uppercut vs. Eye strike: The difference is in intent and training, where a professionally trained boxer is trying to knock someone out, while the drunk college kid is making a desperate attempt. There is also a bit of design wiggle-room for ST's, so that they may determine if they would like the strike to be Lethal or not. As always, I am open to suggestions either way. Accuracy: I am aware of the curve in the numbers regarding dicepools, but difficulty can not drop below 4, ever, for any reason. It's another design choice - giving players an option of adding more dice or lowering difficulty. Smarter players will, of course, lower difficulty any chance they get, but there are still some people that love rolling two handfuls of dice instead. Granularity: I'm not looking to divide, subdivide, further sub-subdivide... As I responded to Phoebus, I'm just trying to provide a list of resources for the players that say &quot;I think an uppercut should do this!&quot; or &quot;I have a melee of 4 and spent 30 years in prison making shanks, of course I know how to use a katana!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: HOD - I think I might erase that sentence about the head and lethal damage. It's supposed to be just flavor-text anyway, and I'm inclined to leave it a little more ambiguous, more open to Storyteller interpretation. Unless empty-handed attacks targeting the head are still bashing? I don't have the books with me right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall seeing anything about bashing being converted to lethal when aimed at the head in the RAW, just that for Kindred, bullets get upgraded from bashing to lethal if aimed at the head. I might be mistaken though.<br /> <br /> As for the intent behind the uppercut vs. eye strike, it sounds like the boxer is going for bashing damage, rather than lethal. After all, dealing lots of lethal damage won't knock people out, it'll kill them. Bashing damage, on the other hand, knocks you out if you're reduced past incap. Now someone poking a finger in your eye, yeah that sounds like they want to do you the kind of harm you'd have to go to the hospital for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T12:05:14-07:00","id":90366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/81969-on-combat?p=89117#post89117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone has a simple i guess &quot;Hack&quot; for improoving &quot;sneak attacks&quot;? just not getting the chance to abort your action so that then you can try to dodge/block/parry doesnt seem like what should be a huge advantage in combat</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, lets be fair here -- getting a round to attack someone in which they cannot take any defensive actions whatsoever, is incredibly powerful. Almost too powerful when you consider that, if all you need to land the attack is a single success (given the fact that neither a dodge nor a parry will be forthcoming) someone could make a called shot to the neck (which is a high diff), but spend a Willpower point to guarantee that it lands. If they can get three health levels past the soak -- that's a decapitation. That's some potent stuff.<br /> <br /> That said, if you feel ambushes should be deadlier still, <i>V:tM </i>(and only <i>V:tM</i>) indicates that, during an ambush attack, one ramps their excess stealth roll successes into their attack.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>For example:</b> Guy is sneaking up on Cop. He rolls dex+stealth (7 dice) vs. Cop's perception+alertness (6 dice). Guy gets 4 successes; Cop gets 2 successes. Now when Guy ambushes Cop, he will add 2 dice to his attack pool.</div> <br /> Just be warned that lots of things tend to get one-shotted when using that rule; but then, that's basically how it is in real life: if you've got the drop on someone, you have an overwhelming advantage over them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T17:51:51-07:00","id":90525,"title":"","content":"I wasn't thinking of a historiography so much as a more informed approach to what weapons can do and what armor can do to protect you from them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2303-phoebus","name":"Phoebus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T14:26:08-07:00","id":91100,"title":"","content":"Internet at home was down for a few days, haven't had time to really work on the doc, and the girlfriend wanted to go see the Veronica Mars movie last night (spoiler: if you like Veronica Mars, you'll like the movie).<br /> <br /> HOD - You are correct, the upgrading from bashing to lethal for targeting the head is for vampires and bullets. That's what I get for transcribing notes from a <i>Vampire</i> game. Changed.<br /> <br /> Phoebus - I'm not overly concerned with armor (I think the books handle that well enough, especially <i>W20</i>), but yes, a practical application of weaponry and accessories is one of the goals. Years ago, I had a player convince me that, in addition to his Quick-draw merit, he kept his .50 Desert Eagle in a Shakespeare - you know, one of those wrist/forearms holsters, usually used for single shots, like derringers? And I allowed it, because I didn't know better (and the internet was not as great a resource as it is now). My intent is for that not to ever happen again, to any Storyteller (because we're a bunch of sad bastards that the players will try any trick on to get ahead).<br /> <br /> Also, both <i>V20</i> and <i>W20 </i>state that mortals cannot soak Lethal damage with just Stamina, so now I need to review my quick combat section...<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T15:07:37-07:00","id":91870,"title":"","content":"Here's what I mean about armor. Certain types of modern armor only protect you from certain calibers of firearms. &quot;Soft armor&quot;, for instance (you know the stuff police wear), won't stop a bullet from an AK-47. The ceramic plates that we wear in Afghanistan <i>will</i> stop such a round, but they are only meant to handle three such shots. Still other forms of armor claim to offer even better protection: Pinnacle's &quot;Dragon Skin&quot; armor, for instance, was supposed to protect from automatic fire/a far greater number of hits from an AK-47/7.62mm round.<br /> <br /> That's quite a bit different from the standing rule, which is that the armor continues to function until the attacker scores a wound that causes a certain amount of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2303-phoebus","name":"Phoebus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T04:38:24-07:00","id":107365,"title":"","content":"The things I am waiting to see / before I comment on stuff:<br /> I will need to go through W20 for armour when I get it in a couple of weeks to see what you mean by that, but I still am anxious to see how you list it (if you do).<br /> <br /> I'm also curious to see if you do anything with shields since the only recourse for those at this point is Dark Ages Vampire (revised). And since you are touching on police / military gear, things like riot shields are a bit more relevant, IMO.<br /> <br /> I am waiting to see more of the mechanics for things. As an example, things like the damage for the Molotov and Thermite. But this is a pretty big project you've got going, and I am quite patient to see how many of the sections come together. As-is, with at least most of the shotgun stuff up it looks quite good for that, especially from the perspective of a Hunter with high Arsenal.<br /> <br /> \u200bLikewise for waiting to see more of how you handle more of the martial maneuvers. I especially am anticipatory towards the wrestling section.<br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Overall, very good work so far.<br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> As to your response to Killersquirrel, yeah, I've had that happen in my group too.<br /> Our Galliard, in a pack with no Ahroun, had built up a damage dice pool of 20. He had 4 successes, and 5 1's, with Charmed Existence to cancel out one of those 1's. A failure, but not a botch. On damage, with a dice pool of 20, at difficulty 6. ... WTF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T05:28:08-07:00","id":107380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZhyzhaksMate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/81969-on-combat?p=107365#post107365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to your response to Killersquirrel, yeah, I've had that happen in my group too.<br /> Our Galliard, in a pack with no Ahroun, had built up a damage dice pool of 20. He had 4 successes, and 5 1's, with Charmed Existence to cancel out one of those 1's. A failure, but not a botch. On damage, with a dice pool of 20, at difficulty 6. ... WTF.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the scene in the movie where the villains navy seal trained body guard can't hit the broad side of a barn with 2 full clips. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T05:41:51-07:00","id":107384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/81969-on-combat?p=107380#post107380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is the scene in the movie where the villains navy seal trained body guard can't hit the broad side of a barn with 2 full clips. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> lol</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to be stuff that happens to that player.<br /> <br /> In a previous game, he was in Zulo form (Viciss 4), Stamina blood-buffed all the way, and a Toredor hit him with a longsword, had a damage dice pool of 14, got 9 successes. If you could botch a soak roll, he would have. Still failed, still lost that character to torpor. Insult-to-injury, to a non-combat Toredor.<br /> <br /> I once (and only once) let him use my dice. Later on, same game (he had a new character) the next roll I had to make was for an enemy lupine pack to step sideways to get into the location of the PC 'tank', with Gnosis 10, and using the Umbral claws fetish (the PC's were already aware of this gear and how OP'ed the pack was, and had the tank bait them away, hoping they could all run like hell). On their 10 dice at difficulty 4 or 5, there were 5 1's rolled... with no successes. This worked out amazingly well for the PC's.<br /> I still don't let that player use my dice anymore. Heck, I don't let him near any dice I plan to use ever.<br /> <br /> Due to the first instance being what it was, we referred to his werewolf failing to damage 'being Toredor'ed', and the title has stuck for those kind of epic fails.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T02:39:56-07:00","id":108052,"title":"","content":"Just skimming it right now as I'm short on time. I'll study it in more detail later, but it looks very promising. I quite like what I've seen of the Fighting Styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T10:02:07-07:00","id":110882,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone, sorry I haven't been around and updating lately. Grading papers, grading papers... you know how it is, real life work got in the way. My schedule's opened up a bit, so I'll go back to tinkering around with the doc and posting updates.<br /> <br /> Thanks again to all of you for taking the time to look over this.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T01:33:09-07:00","id":115165,"title":"","content":"I am afraid I have to be a combo breaker. I disagree, lol.<br /> <br /> I like the direction of stream-lining combat. In my opinion, combat in oWoD is a nightmare to organise. It's very unsatisfying. It's <i>slow as fuck</i>. When I played my first game of Requiem and everything was so easy, that was satisfying. Things moved much more quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T04:06:03-07:00","id":115203,"title":"","content":"All a matter of taste. Combat in my opinion should be slow, and granular enough to apply atmospheric narrative to.<br /> <br /> I played Requiem for two years and found the 'streamlined combat' about as satisfying as flipping a coin to determine the victor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","name":"harlokin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T08:10:11-07:00","id":115283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>harlokin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/81969-on-combat?p=115203#post115203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All a matter of taste. Combat in my opinion should be slow, and granular enough to apply atmospheric narrative to.<br /> <br /> I played Requiem for two years and found the 'streamlined combat' about as satisfying as flipping a coin to determine the victor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Finally someone who agrees with me. You have no idea how long I have searched for someone else who actually likes OWoD combat and its attention to detail.<br /> <br /> <i>Note: Not an edition war, only a praising of what I like about OWoD combat.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T12:19:17-07:00","id":115456,"title":"","content":"I agree. It really is a matter of taste. I personally like to keep die-rolling to a minimum in my games.<br /> <br /> As for this system, I would like it more bare-bones than it is (like Requiem). But I think the aim is to have a happy medium: not quite as roll heavy as Masquerade, but a bit meatier than Requiem. That's what I get from it, anyway.<br /> <br /> I like the ability to split dice pools for multiple actions from Masquerade. I like the expediency of taking turns in Requiem (don't have to go around the table twice to get one person's turn finished, <i>ugh!</i>). Hmm... *reads*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T11:44:44-07:00","id":117559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/81969-on-combat?p=115456#post115456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. It really is a matter of taste. I personally like to keep die-rolling to a minimum in my games.<br /> <br /> As for this system, I would like it more bare-bones than it is (like Requiem). But I think the aim is to have a happy medium: not quite as roll heavy as Masquerade, but a bit meatier than Requiem. That's what I get from it, anyway.<br /> <br /> I like the ability to split dice pools for multiple actions from Masquerade. I like the expediency of taking turns in Requiem (don't have to go around the table twice to get one person's turn finished, <i>ugh!</i>). Hmm... *reads*</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, and thanks to everyone that has taken the time to read this. I am going for leaner cWoD system, but one that's more involved than, say, card games.<br /> <br /> Full disclosure: I have never really &quot;properly&quot; played a nWoD game (which is a shame, because <i>Promethean</i> looks <i>really</i> interesting); the few times I've tried have descended into cWoD with a nWoD skin. This means I lack context and knowledge about the nWoD combat system, so I'm not sure how my system compares. It seems the nWoD system is better built, faster, but less... satisfying, maybe? I don't know.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}